### Page 47 of 84

```text
DDA Strategy 19
Maintain Inventories of Available Downtown Spaces Project Leader:     DDA and DCMA (100)
Logical Partners:  Cheyenne Board of Realtors

Need
• Anecdotal evidence suggests that downtown residents found their
apartments through word-of-mouth or because they rehabilitated
ground floor space and decided to live above the store.
• Most downtown office workers need proximity to other businesses
or City, County and Wyoming government offices.
• If a commercial prospect were to look for available sites in
downtown Cheyenne, they might visit DDA’s web site, but would
probably turn to a broker in search of more complete information.
The DDA maintains a modest list of properties available downtown on
its web site but does not link to the Cheyenne Board of Realtors’ MLS
inventory.  And it doesn’t reflect the variety or competitiveness of space
downtown, with only a few office listings, retail sites and apartments
included.  Moreover, the information is not that easy to find or read.
There needs to be a one-stop clearing house for all downtown space…
retail, office and residential, preferably via a partnership among DDA,
DCMA and the Cheyenne Board of Realtors (CBR).
Remedy
DDA and DCMA should become a resource for brokering downtown
tenancies, including steering prospects to brokers-on-call that can
handle inquiries; DDA/DCMA and the Board of Realtors will need to
develop a mutually acceptable approach.  Currently, the comprehensive
Multiple Listing Service (MLS) site can be sorted for downtown by type
of tenancy, cost, condition, sale or lease, etc.  It should be possible to
fashion a beneficial partnership strengthening the central business
district of Wyoming’s capital that also helps real estate brokers.
Notes
Licensed, professional brokers often offer early insights into
communities’ economic health:  new businesses; new employees; new
residents; new opportunities.  By working with them, DDA and DCMA
can foster more ambassadors for downtown:  a win-win idea.
Specific Tasks
Responsible
Parties
Time
Allowance
Success
Metric
Budget
Allowance
1  Create a wish-list for an initial meeting with the
Cheyenne Board of Realtors.  What can DDA offer CBR
members?  What are some specific opportunities?  What
elements of PlanCheyenne can be leveraged to interest
the real estate broker community?  How will DDA help
increase brokers’ incomes?
2  Compile separate lists of every advantage to
downtown tenancy and/or residency.
3  Schedule the meeting at CBR’s offices.  Propose a
