```text
City Strategy 21

Hide the “Hole”
Project Leader:     City
Logical Partners:  DDA and City Contractors
Need
The Hole is known statewide as
“Cheyenne’s perpetual eyesore.”
By far, it’s the most frequent
complaint about downtown
Cheyenne… and has been since
2004 when a fire gutted Mary’s
Bake Shoppe and other historic storefronts between the Hynds Building
and Wyoming Home.  The site’s multi-party ownership pattern
complicates any quick resolution of what to do next; national economic
uncertainty hasn’t helped.  What could be done to quickly spruce up a
major vehicular entry into downtown?  What needs to enhance the
pedestrian’s experience between the sparkling LightsOn! installation on
the first floor of the Hynds and the retail draws at Wyoming Home,
Lincolnway’s “Women’s Block” and Wrangler – to say nothing of the view
from the Atlas Theater?
Remedy
The City must lead a short-term effort to camouflage this long-standing
eyesore.  In partnership with DDA, the City should embark on a quick,
inexpensive, highly-visible and media-worthy event by installing a three-
story, three dimensional stage set façade on the north side of Lincolnway
between Hynds and Wyoming Home.  This façade –placed on public
property (the sidewalk) – might reflect Beaux Arts, Early Commercial,
Late Victorian or even Moderne styles of architecture.  In fact, several
different stage set facades could be used to test public reaction and
provide guidance on the eventual design of a permanent replacement on
the site (Strategy 27).  Show windows could contain merchandise from
several downtown retailers.  Carefully designed, the façade might even
provide very small spaces for pop-up retail.  This is a temporary
installation – just until a new, permanent development gets underway.
It’s quick and simple.
Notes
Anything that addresses conditions affecting public reaction to
downtown Cheyenne – especially those recognized statewide as
embarrassments – needs to be pursued and faster is better.  Plus, there’s
a precedent for temporary façades just several blocks away – the
Cheyenne Gunslingers stage set on 15th Street at Pioneer.
Specific Tasks
Responsible
Parties
Time
Allowance
Success
Metric

Budget
Allowance

