Determine best-practices as well as pitfalls to
avoid.  Ask for recommendations on
manufacturers and maintenance agreements.
2    Compare manufacturers’ specifications.
3    Test proposals with DCMA member and
all merchants.
4     Discuss pay-station technology with Visit
Cheyenne and the Chamber.  What inventive
programs will make it easy for residents and
visitors to understand and use?
5    In the meantime, thoroughly investigate
the numbers, costs, locations and impacts of
parking for downtown’s 16,400 employees.
Could there be special parking zones and rates
for car-poolers?  Could a Cheyenne Transit
Program offer eShuttle service from some
areas to employment centers via high-
frequency, demand-responsive vans?
6    With Council’s approval, prepare a
