Need
From the start, an unusually large number of artists and craftspeople
participated in the Placemaking project.  It turns out that artisans of all
stripes make up a sizable and active community – much of it centered in
downtown Cheyenne:  over 50 presenting and supporting organizations;
more than 20 galleries and facilities; programs in public and private
schools as well as at LCCC; public art (including the Capitol Avenue
bronzes and 19 Boots Walker installations); a Mayor’s advisory
