Other Strategy 39
Enhance Cheyenne’s Gateways
Project Leader:     MPO
Logical Partners:  WYDOT, WBC, City, DDA,
Service Clubs, etc.
Need
Attractive window displays lure shoppers inside and attest to the
merchant’s pride in the store’s offerings.  The same holds true at larger
scales:  gateways to a city reveal much about how citizens and elected
officials care about attracting outsiders.
Despite downtown Cheyenne’s charms, getting there means passing
through some dreary scenery via Exit 362 on I-80 (South Greeley) and
Exit 9 on I-25 (Lincolnway).  Easy access from two Interstates is a boon,
but these routes to downtown are uneven.  The City, WYDOT and service
groups (notably, Kiwanis) have done a very good job improving these
approaches.  MPO has produced a great set of plans for both. Additional
improvements are in the works in cooperation with WYDOT and Union
Pacific along West Lincolnway.  How can these improvements (and work
recently completed in front of the Dinneen project) be expanded to the
rest of Lincolnway and the I-180 corridor?
Remedy
It’s time to implement MPO’s 2005 plans for both gateways.  Cost
estimates (including contingency) were about $850,000 for Lincolnway
and $1.9 million for I-180/South Greeley (including signs, lighting and
landscape).  Chances are these estimates have not increased
dramatically.  The plans also included a realistic sources-of-funds section.
Major points:
• Apply for federal transportation enhancement funds administered by
WYDOT (Transportation Enhancement Activities – Local, or TEAL) in a
roughly 90 percent federal, ten percent State and City formula;
• Continue partnering with Union Pacific.  UP owns land on Lincolnway
and I-180 passes over the massive UP yards;
• Submit a Business Ready Community Grant to the Wyoming Business
Council “…to improve the community’s aesthetic character… to make
itself more attractive for business development.”
Notes
Lincolnway and South Greeley are the primary gateways – front yards –
into downtown .  In turn, downtown Cheyenne is the gateway – the front
porch – to the State Capitol.  “What the neighbors think“ is important.
Improve Lincolnway and I-180 as ways to get to downtown, not just
through it.
