Other Strategy 41
Plan Cheyenne’s 150th Birthday: July 4, 2017
Project Leader:     A New “Cheyenne 150” Group
Logical Partners:  Everyone
Need
What happened here almost 150 years ago is still a vivid and evolving
part of the American saga – the wild west, the transcontinental railroad,
“Hell on Wheels,” cowboys and cowgirls, “Equality State,” boom and
bust and boom again, “Magic City of the Plains,” the new West, the next
West…  In four years, Cheyenne will celebrate a birthday – its first 150
years.  It won’t do to wait until 2017 to plan a celebration.  Start now!
Remedy
Think of Strategy 1 as a series of dress rehearsals for the really big event.
The City should charter a totally inclusive “Cheyenne 150” nonprofit
organization and give it sole responsibility to plan, organize, coordinate,
implement and manage a year-long commemoration that 1) showcases
the past, 2) celebrates today’s Cheyenne and 3) guarantees Cheyenne’s
promise tomorrow.  Cheyenne 150 might:
• Adopt 15 strategies suggested in this Placemaking document for
completions and ribbon cuttings.  For example, add 15 new
downtown arts, culture and food festivals – to be continued beyond
2017 (e.g., High Plains cook-offs using heritage recipes, traditional
Native American foods, Intercontinental Hotel menu tastings, etc.;
• Start a CheyenneCorps intern program for Wyoming’s budding
architects, engineers, craftspeople, environmentalists,
archaeologists, etc., to restore facades, buildings and artifacts (e.g.,
UP engines and rolling stock);
• Host the 2017 edition of the Indigenous Native American Games, an
affiliate of the US Olympics Committee.  (Past INAG games attracted
10,000 athletes from 1,000 tribes in the US and Canada);
• Plan a National Main Street conference for the 16 other state capitals
that are also Main Street communities to identify common
strategies.  Test them in Cheyenne;
• Hold 5th, 10th… reunions for the three high schools and LCCC;
• Celebrate the various modes of transport that opened Cheyenne:
horses; mule teams; stage coaches; vintage 1917 cars and trucks; UP
rolling stock, etc.
Notes
This is much too big a milestone to ignore!
Specific Tasks
Responsible
Parties
Time
Allowance
Success
Metric
Budget
Allowance
