be either coupon bonds or bonds registrable as to principal, or
principal and interest, or both.

(e)  If lost or completely destroyed, any security authorized by
this article may be reissued in the form and tenor of the lost or
destroyed security upon the owner furnishing, to the satisfaction of the
governing body, proof of ownership; proof of loss or destruction; a
surety bond in twice the face amount of the security, including any
unmatured coupons appertaining thereto; and payment of the cost of
preparing and issuing the new security.

(f)  Any officer authorized to execute any bond, after filing with
the secretary of state his manual signature certified by him under oath,
may execute or cause to be executed, with a facsimile signature in lieu
